WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.222
Welcome to Module 5. Lists and tuples organize values by position.

00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:09.872
Dictionaries and sets give us two new ideas: labels and uniqueness.

00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:19.147
A dictionary stores key-value pairs, so instead of remembering that a value is at position two,

00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:22.152
we can retrieve it by a meaningful label.

00:00:22.152 --> 00:00:25.457
A set automatically keeps unique values.

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:34.803
These structures are extremely useful for records, category counts, lookup tables, unique IDs, and data-cleaning tasks.
